## 1. Executive Summary & Experiment Hypothesis

### 1.1 Context
We are upgrading the mobile betslip stake entry experience from the legacy 6×2 grid layout to a standardized 3×4 numerical thumb-zone layout. 
Concurrently, we are executing an A/B/n experiment evaluating the ergonomic positioning of the primary "Place Bet" Call to Action (CTA) relative to the on-screen keypad to maximize bet throughput.

### 1.2 Primary Hypothesis
Positioning the "Place Bet" CTA directly adjacent to the thumb strike zone during stake entry reduces eye-travel and thumb repositioning latency, driving a statistically significant uplift in **Betslip Conversion Rate** (specifically on fast-moving in-play markets) without increasing accidental bet placement slips.

---

## 2. Experiment Matrix & Variant Definitions

Eligible mobile sessions are allocated evenly across three variants via the feature flag `exp_betslip_keypad_cta_layout`:

| Dimension | Control Group | Variant A (`cta_above`) | Variant B (`cta_below`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Keypad Grid** | Legacy 6×2 layout| Standard 3×4 layout| Standard 3×4 layout|
| **Place Bet CTA Position** | Pinned to bottom of betslip container below keypad| Stacked **directly above** quick-stake chips | Stacked **directly below** numeric grid (bottom of keypad container)|
| **Keypad Trigger** | Stake field focus / blur| Stake field focus / blur| Stake field focus / blur|
| **Quick Stake Chips** | Horizontal chips above keypad| Horizontal chips above keypad | Horizontal chips above the keypad|

